io"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overact ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to exaggerate an action", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Megan, you are overreacting! There are only eight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "appear ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to exist; to act", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: NULL has appeared automatically many times when using PHP.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "explicitly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "referring to directly; straight forward", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a rule, it must always be explicitly declared, or it won't work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "suppose ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to assume; to expect", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: No one would suppose PHP needs considerable expertise since beginners have been using it for a while now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose 5 data types that you liked the most and research more about them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write their functions and characteristics, and provide 3 examples for each data type.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your examples and the new information you found to one of your classmates.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for more information about 5 data types.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write their functions and characteristics and provide 3 examples for each type. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with a classmate. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modal Verbs for Speculating: Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <b>would</b> to talk about hypothetical events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we want to talk about events in the future that are hypothetical, we can use the modal verb <strong>would.</strong> These events are not very likely to take place; that's why, it's necessary to express probability and not certainty.</br></br>  Let's take a look at the structure:</br></br>  <div align=\"center\">Subject + <strong>would</strong> + verb in base form+ complement</div></br>  Examples:</br><i> She <strong>would</strong> work as an engineer, but she doesn't know the PHP data types.</br> This program <strong>would</strong> run better with PHP object, but there is an object declared. </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I wouldn't have thought you were so good at remembering numbers until now! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I thought they would be more difficult.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Null Value and Resource Data Type in PHP", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are two special data types in PHP: <strong>Null value</strong> and <strong>Resource data.</strong>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>NULL Value</strong></br> Null is special because it can only have one value. As its name suggests that value is NULL. You could think it is the same as having a value of zero, but it's not.</br></br>  When you create a variable, but do not assign a value to it; automatically, it is assigned a <strong>Null</strong> value, which is very different from writing zero as a value. </br> Also, when you set another variable to be <strong>NULL</strong>, the variable data will be emptied.</br></br>  <strong>PHP Resource </strong></br> It is not exactly a data type. PHP Resource stores a reference to operations and resources that are external to PHP. </br> A good example of this data type is a database call.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can list data types PHP supports.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can present information about data types like Boolean, array or object.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about data types like string, integer or support.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What data types from other languages do you know? Why do we use them for? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you think the advantages of PHP data types are?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Relevant Information About Data Types", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "type": "WLC"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Leo and Megan talk about the data types in PHP.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]},